Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.27 / P6.28 Quit game on the title menu, Return to title in the field menu

P6.27 / P6.28: the title menu's fourth row, Quit game, and the field menu's
Return to title row, each behind a Yes / No window (port/options/confirm.c).

Title menu (src/menus/title/menu.c): with the native overlay the Down limit
moves from Continue to Quit game (DW3_TITLE_QUIT, row 3); Cross on it opens
the window with the cursor on No and the menu takes no input until it is
answered (the Port options screen's pattern: the window is ticked by the
menu task, only on a frame after the one that opened it). Without the native
overlay nothing changes (dw3_port_title_quit_enabled() is 0).

Field menu (src/engine/menu/field_menu.c, include/engine/menu.h): while the
Restart hotkey setting is ON (P6.9's opt-in, off by default), the options
list has one more row, the last, with the text of dw3_port_field_return_label()
in the game's own font encoding. The options panel is the next one up (the
six-row sprite 0x1B for the five rows plus this one); with the card folders
row there are seven rows and the game has no panel for that, so the six-row
panel's bottom edge is covered and redrawn one row lower with five TILEs in
the panel's colours (drawFieldMenuPanelRow, submitted before the sprite so the
ordering table draws it in front). Cross on the row opens the window; the
menu waits while it is up. A Yes asks the P6.9 reset (dw3_port_restart_request,
same flush, a failed flush cancels). With the setting OFF nothing is added and
the drawing calls are the ones of the game (no replay reference changes).
FieldMenuWindows.options grows from six to seven windows (PORT_HOST only).

